{
  "text": " Going to Europe this fall? Don't check a bag for Paris, Milan, and London. I pack one Weekender, and it goes in the overhead bin. This is the Eleanor Weekender from Volantra. Paris is where you pack less. Pieces that work together. So three days of clothes fit in here, and the flap folds all the way back so I can see everything. Milan is where it gets polished and intentional. Full grain leather over woven canvas, real brass hardware, no logo anywhere, and it keeps its shape, packed full or barely at all. London is where you walk all day and it's four seasons in one day. So the knitwear and the coat come too and it still keeps its shape. I've dragged mine through three airports and it still looks new. It comes in four colors and the black one is a pre-order that ships mid-September. They're running a sale on it right now and the colors go fast. So grab it before the trip. So tell me, Paris, Milan, or London? Which one are you packing for? I left the link below.",
